---
title: M-Ranked — VK collection sequence
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant S as Scheduler
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant V as VK adapter
    participant VK as VK API
    participant P as Canonical pipeline
    participant R as Redis

    S->>R: Acquire vk partition lease
    S->>DB: Start collection_run and load enabled VK accounts
    loop For each account within account concurrency limit
        S->>V: collect(account)
        V->>VK: groups.getById(fields=members_count)
        VK-->>V: Community ID, screen name, title, members
        V->>VK: wall.get(owner, max 100, without pinned)
        VK-->>V: Recent wall posts and counters
        V->>V: Resolve ordinary vs joint-post canonical identity
        V->>DB: Load active stored publications and last snapshots
        V->>V: Select due posts absent from current wall page
        loop Batches up to 100 IDs
            V->>VK: wall.getById(source external IDs)
            VK-->>V: Existing posts, deleted/missing omitted
        end
        V->>P: Discovered + refreshed posts and missing probes
        P->>P: Normalize views, likes, comments and reposts
        P->>P: Convert transient positive-to-zero reset into NULL + quality flag
        P->>P: Preserve measured zero when no reset evidence exists
        P->>P: Increment missing confirmation, mark deleted only at threshold
        P->>DB: Transactional account metadata, publications, snapshots and deletion probes
        DB-->>P: Commit with dataset revision
        P->>R: Publish revision.changed after commit
        P->>DB: Complete account result
    end
    S->>DB: Complete collection_run with API/error counts
    S->>R: Release/expire lease

    Note over V,VK: VK rate limiter serializes API calls to the configured requests-per-second limit.
    Note over P,DB: source_external_id is retained for joint posts and stable public URLs.
